# Windsurf Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: React with TypeScript
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS
- **State Management**: Zustand (authStore)
- **Data Fetching**: React Query (@tanstack/react-query)
- **Routing**: React Router
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod
- **Icons**: Lucide React
- **Animations**: Framer Motion
- **Build Tool**: Vite

## Code Style
- Use functional components with hooks
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Keep components small and focused
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Follow existing naming conventions (camelCase for variables, PascalCase for components)
- Use meaningful variable and function names

## File Structure
- `src/components/` - Reusable UI components
- `src/pages/` - Page-level components
- `src/lib/` - Utilities, API clients, types
- `src/hooks/` - Custom React hooks
- `src/store/` - Zustand stores
- `src/layouts/` - Layout components

## API Integration
- Use the `apiRequest` function from `src/lib/base.ts` for all API calls
- Store tokens in `authStore` and localStorage
- Use React Query for data fetching and caching
- Handle errors gracefully with user-friendly messages

## Styling Guidelines
- Use Tailwind CSS for all styling
- Follow the existing design system (colors, spacing, typography)
- Use the `font-cairo` font for Arabic text
- Ensure RTL support for Arabic content
- Make components responsive (mobile-first approach)

## Testing
- Write unit tests for critical business logic
- Test API endpoints
- Ensure accessibility (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation)

## Git Workflow
- Write clear, descriptive commit messages
- Use feature branches for new features
- Keep commits atomic and focused
